Author: Devuser <hi@devuser.nu>
Date:   Fri Jul 10 05:44:38 2026 +0200

    fix(feed): mint article ids from the deduped filename stem

    persistArticle built the article id from the bare title slug before the
    filename dedup loop ran, so two same-title/same-day/same-site articles
    without a published date could share one id even though they got
    separate files; the corpus already has 20 such colliding groups.
    The id now derives from the final deduped filename so every written
    file and its id stay in one-to-one correspondence.

